{
  "id": 302560605,
  "iid": 15669,
  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "UDP: Fix level of hierarchy for the payload subtree",
  "description": "Until now, subtrees esteeming from UDP payload are always added at the root layer. While this is okay for the most packets (as every packet layer is at the root level), it is wrong, inconsistent and misleading when the UDP packet is a subtree already (e.g. in a copy of original packet in a ICMP Destination Unreachable message).\n\nThis patch aims to fix this. While this does not affect display filter, some exports might be affected.\n\n### Visual example\n\nFile:  \n[wireshark_udp_subtrees.pcapng](/uploads/b087ace5959a52fc798e38d6ac7819b4/wireshark_udp_subtrees.pcapng)\n\nBefore:\\\n![wireshark_udp_subtrees_before](/uploads/12a92fb84f5a8e69aab7889ccfe6b7ce/wireshark_udp_subtrees_before.png)\n\nExpected/After:\\\n![wireshark_udp_subtrees_expected](/uploads/751a85ff64c4dd1ade54dccfbb7a597c/wireshark_udp_subtrees_expected.png)",
