      "title": "UDP: Correct level of hierarchy for the payload subtree",
      "message": "UDP: Correct level of hierarchy for the payload subtree\n\nPreviously, subtrees steeming from UDP payload are always added at the root\nlayer. While this is okay for the most packets (everything is at the root\nlevel), it is wrong and misleading when the UDP packet is a subtree already\n(e.g. in a copy of original packet in a ICMP Destination Unreachable message).\n\nVisualisation of an exemplary ICMP message for a STUN packet to closed port\n\nBefore:\n- IP\n- ICMP Destination Unreachable\n-- IP\n-- UDP\n- STUN\n\nAfter:\n- IP\n- ICMP Destination Unreachable\n-- IP\n-- UDP\n-- STUN\n",
      "author_name": "Thomas Vogt",
      "author_email": "gitwiresharktv@ist-einmalig.de",
      "authored_date": "2024-05-17T14:13:12.000+02:00",
      "committer_name": "AndersBroman",
      "committer_email": "a.broman58@gmail.com",
